wed Crane ahead by only two points, and prediction markets give Nez roughly a one-in-three chance of winning. Nez has campaigned on water access and cost-of-living issues, and outside groups have spent against Crane. Still, the partisan lean and incumbency make Crane the clear favorite, with real but limited downside risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1703, "margin": -5.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2296, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2721, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1924, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2064, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2601, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2994, "margin": -4.0}]}